.TH HEAD 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
head \- affiche le debut des fichiers / output the first part of files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B head
[-n N] [-c N] [-qv] [file...]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the first 10 lines of each file. With -n -N prints all but the last N lines.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -n N
First N lines.
.TP
.B -c N
First N bytes.
.TP
.B -q
Never print headers.
.TP
.B -v
Always print headers.
.SH SEE ALSO
tail(1)
